# {{pascalCase project.name}} Web

A small, standalone Angular application with a feature-first structure, signal-based UI state, and a development proxy for the Spring Boot API.

## Requirements

- Node.js 22.22.3 or later in the 22.x line, 24.15.0 or later in the 24.x line, or 26.0.0 or later in the 26.x line
- npm

## Start developing

```bash
npm install
npm start
```

The frontend is served at `http://localhost:4200`. Requests under `/api` are proxied to the backend at `http://localhost:8080`.

## Build

```bash
npm run build
```

The production build is written to `dist/{{kebabCase project.name}}-web/browser`.

## Structure

```text
src/app/
  api/                 OpenAPI client placeholder
  core/                Application-wide services and layout
  features/            Route-level product features
  app.config.ts        Application providers
  app.routes.ts        Lazy-loaded routes
```

Angular components are standalone. The app uses Angular signals and built-in `@if` / `@for` template control flow. Angular 22 enables zoneless change detection by default.

## API client

See `src/app/api/README.md` for the planned OpenAPI-generated client location and regeneration command.
